tap-to-mac
==========

This product includes software inspired by and depending on work from the
following open-source projects.


taigrr/spank
------------
https://github.com/taigrr/spank
License: MIT

The idea of using the Apple Silicon IMU to detect physical hits on the laptop
comes from spank. tap-to-mac borrows the same hardware approach and re-uses
spank's accelerometer library directly. Thanks to taigrr for the original work
and for spinning the IMU reader out as a reusable library.


taigrr/apple-silicon-accelerometer
----------------------------------
https://github.com/taigrr/apple-silicon-accelerometer
License: MIT
Copyright (c) 2026 olvvier

tap-to-mac depends on this library for IOKit HID access, the shared-memory
ring buffer, and the upstream vibration detector. It is pulled in as a normal
Go module via go.mod; no source is vendored.
